WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.434
The Man Who Can’t Breathe is probably the most mysterious paranormal entity

00:00:03.482 --> 00:00:04.810
in the Insidious franchise.

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:08.206
Not much is known about his history or backstory, but by studying his

00:00:08.228 --> 00:00:10.830
appearance and his victims, we can learn more about him.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.966
Like in my analysis of The Red Face Demon, there's a major clue about his

00:00:13.988 --> 00:00:17.546
origin hiding in plain sight. The Man Who Can’t Breathe is a grimy, sickly

00:00:17.578 --> 00:00:20.794
looking creature with an oxygen mask over his gaping hole of a mouth.

00:00:20.842 --> 00:00:24.058
The Respiratory Care Journal states that the first cylinders for storing

00:00:24.074 --> 00:00:28.610
oxygen were developed in 1868, which allowed its use in general anesthesia.

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:31.974
This means that The Man Who Can't Breathe, at least in his current form,

00:00:32.012 --> 00:00:33.670
is less than 140 years old.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:37.046
It is possible that he existed before that because he does demonstrate the

00:00:37.068 --> 00:00:39.942
ability to shape shift, but chances are that we'll never know.

00:00:39.996 --> 00:00:43.078
For all intents and purposes, the oxygen mask form is what we're concerned

00:00:43.094 --> 00:00:44.070
with for this lesson.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:47.946
The Red Face Demon's bright, bold, almost carnival appearance was for the

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:51.702
purpose of deceiving curious children, thereby luring them into The Further.

00:00:51.766 --> 00:00:54.430
But this evil spirit has a different goal.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:59.646
-[Elise] Usually, entities of this type living in the dark, they want to possess the

00:00:59.668 --> 00:01:04.846
-[Elise] bodies of the living so that they can leave the dark and return to life.

00:01:05.028 --> 00:01:06.830
-[Elise] There's another kind of spirit.

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:11.394
-[Elise] It's an even worse kind, one that does not want to leave the dark, 

00:01:11.432 --> 00:01:14.926
-[Elise] that wants the souls of the living to join it in the shadows.

00:01:15.038 --> 00:01:18.626
So it's likely that The Man Who Can’t Breathe's frail visage is intended to

00:01:18.648 --> 00:01:22.006
garner sympathy from the victims and maybe even remind them of

00:01:22.028 --> 00:01:22.994
someone they know who has suffered.

00:01:23.042 --> 00:01:27.078
In 2007, that's exactly what happened to Quinn Brenner and her family.

00:01:27.164 --> 00:01:30.294
To learn about the other victims of The Man Who Can’t Breathe, how he gains

00:01:30.342 --> 00:01:33.782
power over them, and if he could return in a future Insidious installment.

00:01:33.846 --> 00:01:36.140
Stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:41.915
♪ Metal Music ♪

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:43.726
Welcome to Horror History.

00:01:43.828 --> 00:01:47.326
Everyone said that Red Face looked like Darth Maul, so why not create an

00:01:47.348 --> 00:01:49.710
antagonist that sounds like Darth Vader?

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:53.087
(Breathing sound)

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.410
I just hope they don't make one that smells like Darth Sidious.

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:59.602
The Man Who Can’t Breathe's only appearance was in Insidious: Chapter3 ,

00:01:59.656 --> 00:02:02.866
which centers around Quinn Brenner, a girl mourning the death of her mom and

00:02:02.888 --> 00:02:05.986
suffering the effects of the lack of motherly guidance as

00:02:06.008 --> 00:02:07.182
she's trying to break out into adulthood.

00:02:07.246 --> 00:02:10.326
To reflect the circumstances, writer director Leigh Whannell created

00:02:10.348 --> 00:02:13.446
The Man Who Can't Breathe as an embodiment of cancer and the kind of

00:02:13.468 --> 00:02:15.878
misery and misfortune that can damper a person's life in general.

00:02:15.964 --> 00:02:19.858
-[Leigh] I actually said to the special effects makeup team who was creating him,

00:02:19.884 --> 00:02:25.913
-[Leigh] I said, imagine if cancer, the disease, was a person. What would he look like? 

00:02:25.913 --> 00:02:27.286
And that look was realized by special makeup

00:02:27.318 --> 00:02:30.456
effects creator Justin Raleigh. As for his canvas...

00:02:30.538 --> 00:02:32.858
-[Leigh] I remember saying to Terry, the casting agent, I was like,

00:02:32.864 --> 00:02:36.366
-[Leigh] you know, I want someone like that guy from Se7en he should look like

00:02:36.388 --> 00:02:37.434
-[Leigh] he's on the verge of death.

00:02:37.482 --> 00:02:39.898
And that's the exact guy they got, Michael Reid MacKay, 

00:02:39.914 --> 00:02:43.082
but this time, instead of the victim, he took the role of the villain.

00:02:43.146 --> 00:02:45.866
There's actually some confusion, though, about what

00:02:45.898 --> 00:02:46.958
The Man Who Can't Breathe really is.

00:02:47.044 --> 00:02:52.063
Is he some kind of vengeful ghost or a demon? An entity who is never human to begin with? 

00:02:52.063 --> 00:02:54.034
To answer that question and the other mysteries of this

00:02:54.072 --> 00:02:57.350
character, I'm going to take it back to some of his earlier victims.

00:02:57.350 --> 00:03:02.095
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.286
The Fleur De Lis Apartments, where The Man Who Can’t Breathe seems to be

00:03:05.308 --> 00:03:08.886
situated, were built in 1930, and it seems he has roughly seven or eight

00:03:08.908 --> 00:03:12.266
victims spread over the time since then, although most of them look more

00:03:12.288 --> 00:03:15.130
modern, like this woman who's not interested in talking.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:16.858
-[Ghost Woman] Get away from me.

00:03:17.024 --> 00:03:20.394
And this girl Danielle, who says that The Man Who Can’t Breathe made her

00:03:20.432 --> 00:03:21.110
kill herself.

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:24.186
I'm guessing she was the most recent victim before the entity attached

00:03:24.218 --> 00:03:25.210
itself to Quinn.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:28.206
-[Danielle] Where was his bed? He's got a new bed.

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:29.758
-[Danielle]There's no end to it.

00:03:29.924 --> 00:03:32.142
-[Danielle] You can't even kill yourself to get away from it.

00:03:32.196 --> 00:03:34.558
This is The Man Who Can’t Breathe his main source of attack.

00:03:34.644 --> 00:03:37.906
He goes after people dealing with depression and tries to manipulate them

00:03:37.928 --> 00:03:40.590
into ending it so that they will join him in the dark forever.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:42.894
He's essentially hoarding and collecting souls.

00:03:42.942 --> 00:03:45.662
The end of their lives does not equal the end of their misery.

00:03:45.726 --> 00:03:48.962
Danielle exists in a perpetual state of rain, a weather pattern often

00:03:49.016 --> 00:03:50.290
associated with depression.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:54.674
The table is set for his next target in late 2005, when Quinn's mom,

00:03:54.722 --> 00:03:56.482
Lilith Brenner, passed away from lung cancer.

00:03:56.546 --> 00:03:59.606
It's easy to imagine at the end, she probably didn't look too different from

00:03:59.628 --> 00:04:02.426
The Man Who Can’t Breathe, making it a little harder for Quinn to

00:04:02.448 --> 00:04:05.466
differentiate between the two when she's later visited by the entity,

00:04:05.488 --> 00:04:08.841
which would happen around spring 2007, approximately. 

00:04:08.841 --> 00:04:11.898
-[Quinn] Like at night, I'll be in my room or I'll be asleep and

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:13.114
-[Quinn] something will wake me up.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:17.050
-[Quinn] I'll find things in weird places, like I'll find my diary somewhere strange.

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:19.726
At first, Quinn thought her mother was trying to reach her from the

00:04:19.748 --> 00:04:21.262
afterlife, which she actually was.

00:04:21.316 --> 00:04:24.170
She wanted Quinn to find the letter she had left in the back of her diary.

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:28.174
However, the entity waking her up in the night was not her mom, which meant

00:04:28.222 --> 00:04:30.674
trouble when Quinn tried to make contact on her own.

00:04:30.712 --> 00:04:33.618
And this is when The Man Who Can’t Breathe attached himself to her.

00:04:33.704 --> 00:04:36.946
Eventually, she visited psychic medium Elise Rainier for help reaching her mother.

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:40.402
But Elise ends up making contact with something far more dangerous.

00:04:40.466 --> 00:04:42.418
Possibly The Man Who Can’t Breathe.

00:04:42.514 --> 00:04:45.110
-[Elise] You have to be very careful.

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:49.910
-[Elise] If you call out to one of the dead, all of them can hear you.

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:53.286
Elise likely senses that something has attached itself to her and suggests

00:04:53.318 --> 00:04:56.714
that she go see another psychic, not realizing that this encounter has also

00:04:56.752 --> 00:04:58.170
attached the demon to her.

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:02.266
Quinn goes home and immediately ignores Elise's advice by calling out to her mom.

00:05:02.288 --> 00:05:05.538
This is where you'd probably expect me to dunk on her, but she's

00:05:05.574 --> 00:05:07.166
desperate to talk to her mom again.

00:05:07.268 --> 00:05:07.806
I get it.

00:05:07.828 --> 00:05:09.802
I'll save my rant for someone more deserving.

00:05:09.866 --> 00:05:13.178
She senses something in her air vents, and since The Man Who Can’t Breathe's

00:05:13.194 --> 00:05:16.398
domain is this building, the ventilation system seems to be an avenue for

00:05:16.404 --> 00:05:17.118
him to get around.

00:05:17.204 --> 00:05:20.154
He follows her that morning to an audition that she's doing for a theater school

00:05:20.202 --> 00:05:23.326
and waves to her on top of a catwalk right as she's calling on her

00:05:23.348 --> 00:05:25.090
mom to help get her through the audition.

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:28.726
However, she botches the audition, and that night, as she's headed home with

00:05:28.748 --> 00:05:32.054
her friend, he appears to her again as she's crossing the street,

00:05:32.092 --> 00:05:35.606
which distracts her from some psychopath attempting to murder her with a car.

00:05:35.708 --> 00:05:39.394
She somehow manages to survive, but she's knocked into a temporary coma,

00:05:39.442 --> 00:05:42.566
during which she travels to The Further and finds herself in a black void,

00:05:42.598 --> 00:05:46.380
where she encounters her otherworldly stalker up close for the first time.

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:51.290
This has probably the opposite intended effect and jolts her awake.

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:54.318
But when she's finally healed enough to go back home, she would find that

00:05:54.324 --> 00:05:56.954
she is not safe from this suffocating stranger.

00:05:57.082 --> 00:06:02.580
-[Grace] The Man Who Can’t Breathe. The man who lives in the vents.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:05.620
-[Grace] I heard him saying your name last night.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:09.370
(Impact)

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:13.266
As many of you know, being a creator is more to me than just making content.

00:06:13.368 --> 00:06:15.694
You guys see me in other comment sections, at events,

00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:17.138
I'm all about that creator life.

00:06:17.224 --> 00:06:20.146
That's why I was really excited when Youtooz reached out about doing a

00:06:20.168 --> 00:06:23.506
CZsWorld vinyl figure, because I had seen my favorite creators release

00:06:23.538 --> 00:06:24.790
Youtooz figures over the years.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:27.654
So to me, this was more than just a cool merchandise opportunity.

00:06:27.772 --> 00:06:29.170
This was a rite of passage.

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:32.650
I wanted to make my Youtooz the greatest one of all time, so I did.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:35.882
The CZsWorld Youtooz combines my classic Horror History get up,

00:06:35.936 --> 00:06:40.054
complete with Overlook Hotel carpet pattern tie with the iconic CZsWorld logo mask.

00:06:40.102 --> 00:06:42.762
We really went all in on the details for this, not just on the figure itself,

00:06:42.816 --> 00:06:46.218
but the entire box and presentation is premium artwork.

00:06:46.314 --> 00:06:49.274
And because of that, it's only going to be available for a very limited time.

00:06:49.322 --> 00:06:51.978
Once these are gone, they're gone forever.

00:06:52.074 --> 00:06:54.558
Unless you want to be shelling out millions of dollars to get one of these

00:06:54.564 --> 00:06:57.246
on eBay in the future, I'd recommend you pick it up now by clicking that

00:06:57.268 --> 00:06:58.202
link in the description.

00:06:58.266 --> 00:07:00.926
I'm super excited to announce that these are now available, and I'm looking

00:07:00.948 --> 00:07:03.514
forward to seeing what the CZsWorld community does with their Youtooz.

00:07:03.562 --> 00:07:06.146
So make sure and send me those pictures on social media once you receive them.

00:07:06.178 --> 00:07:10.150
You too can take home a piece of CZsWorld with Youtooz.

00:07:11.695 --> 00:07:15.000
♪ Haunting Music ♪

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:17.542
As Quinn tries to get some sleep, in her own bed.

00:07:17.596 --> 00:07:20.130
The Man Who Can’t Breathe looms over her menacingly.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:24.266
We can only speculate if his plan was to make her a traffic fatality, or if

00:07:24.288 --> 00:07:27.674
he simply wanted to break her spirit with another tragedy, thus making it

00:07:27.712 --> 00:07:29.142
easier to absorb her soul.

00:07:29.206 --> 00:07:32.586
As he gets closer, Quinn's dad, Sean Brenner, comes in and turns on the lights,

00:07:32.608 --> 00:07:35.466
which seems to cause The Man Who Can’t Breathe to dissipate.

00:07:35.578 --> 00:07:38.926
There are multiple examples of him disappearing in the light, which falls in

00:07:38.948 --> 00:07:39.882
line with his character.

00:07:39.946 --> 00:07:43.626
Depression is often described as a deep darkness, and light can literally

00:07:43.658 --> 00:07:44.462
help cure it.

00:07:44.516 --> 00:07:48.114
It goes further, no pun intended, because the light and dark are also used

00:07:48.152 --> 00:07:51.586
to refer to the real world and The Further in the Insidious franchise,

00:07:51.608 --> 00:07:53.230
the dark is literally his domain.

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:55.634
The following evening, he continues to try to break her.

00:07:55.672 --> 00:07:58.798
She knocks on her neighbor's wall, and he knocks back, but she quickly finds

00:07:58.814 --> 00:08:00.726
out that her neighbor wasn't actually home.

00:08:00.828 --> 00:08:02.530
This is the weirdest part of the movie.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:06.214
She asks if she woke him up, and he responds with, I'm not at home,

00:08:06.252 --> 00:08:07.318
which doesn't answer the question.

00:08:07.404 --> 00:08:10.134
I get that the point was for the audience to learn that it wasn't him

00:08:10.172 --> 00:08:13.206
knocking on the wall, but from Hector's point of view, he doesn't even know

00:08:13.228 --> 00:08:16.006
that she knocked on the wall if he's not home, so he should have just

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:16.790
answered the question.

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:18.754
That's basically my only gripe with this movie.

00:08:18.802 --> 00:08:20.110
This scene doesn't make sense.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.910
After Quinn has turned off the lights, he attacks her in a much more direct manner.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:26.046
In addition to being able to use the air vents to travel, he has the

00:08:26.068 --> 00:08:28.394
ability to walk on walls and hang from the ceiling.

00:08:28.442 --> 00:08:31.274
So he shockingly grabs her from above, causing her to scream

00:08:31.322 --> 00:08:34.958
as cracks permeate on the ceiling. Her dad hears the commotion and takes the

00:08:34.964 --> 00:08:38.338
manager up to the fifth floor, where he finds black, tarry footprints in the

00:08:38.344 --> 00:08:41.234
room directly above Quinn's room continuing on under the bed.

00:08:41.234 --> 00:08:42.814
It seems that he's using the uninhabited

00:08:42.862 --> 00:08:44.878
upstairs apartment as a base of operation.

00:08:44.974 --> 00:08:48.446
Sensing Quinn's troubles, a guilty Elise tries to reach out to Lily Brenner

00:08:48.478 --> 00:08:51.606
the next night, but once again only manages to draw the attention of the demon.

00:08:51.628 --> 00:08:53.890
And yes, I do mean demon.

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:57.254
After following a new set of black footprints through her home to find her

00:08:57.292 --> 00:09:00.998
psychic reading room somehow unlocked, Elise announces that she is unafraid.

00:09:01.094 --> 00:09:03.670
-[Elise] I've fought many like you in my time, demon.

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:07.302
There's some inconsistency when it comes to identifying this antagonist.

00:09:07.366 --> 00:09:10.826
A demon is an inhuman spirit, whereas a ghost is the spirit of a human who

00:09:10.848 --> 00:09:11.450
passed away.

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:15.262
The Red Face Demon was obviously a demon, as opposed to The Bride in Black,

00:09:15.316 --> 00:09:17.354
who was a person who eventually became a ghost.

00:09:17.402 --> 00:09:22.400
Elise refers to The Man Who Can’t Breathe as a demon at first, but later says this

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:24.954
-[Elise] This entity is very powerful.

00:09:25.082 --> 00:09:28.674
-[Elise] It's a spirit who used to live in this building a long time ago.

00:09:28.712 --> 00:09:30.782
Before eventually going back to calling it a demon.

00:09:30.846 --> 00:09:33.422
So which one is it? In an interview with Collider.

00:09:33.486 --> 00:09:36.866
Leigh Whannell was asked if this new entity was more like Red Face or more like

00:09:36.888 --> 00:09:38.994
the Bride to which he says this.

00:09:39.112 --> 00:09:43.522
-[Leigh] I would say he's more in line with the fire faced demon from the first film.

00:09:43.586 --> 00:09:47.106
And in the making of documentary at Macabre Creations, he seems to imply

00:09:47.138 --> 00:09:49.703
that there is a demon in Insidious: Chapter 3.

00:09:49.703 --> 00:09:52.822
-[Leigh] In an Insidious film, your demons are your bread and butter.

00:09:52.886 --> 00:09:55.946
On top of that, there are only two creatures who demonstrate the wall

00:09:55.968 --> 00:09:58.982
crawling ability The Red Face Demon and The Man Who Can’t Breathe.

00:09:59.046 --> 00:10:02.614
I think the name The MAN Who Can’t Breathe refers to this particular demon

00:10:02.662 --> 00:10:04.502
taking on a more humanoid appearance.

00:10:04.566 --> 00:10:07.278
And when Elise says that he's a spirit that used to live in the building a

00:10:07.284 --> 00:10:10.286
long time ago, I don't know, maybe his appearance is based on someone who

00:10:10.308 --> 00:10:11.230
once lived in the building.

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:13.966
Or maybe that's just like something she made up to make herself look more credible.

00:10:13.988 --> 00:10:14.974
I don't know.

00:10:15.012 --> 00:10:17.966
Or how about this? Maybe when she said he lived in the building, she just

00:10:17.988 --> 00:10:19.342
meant that he inhabits the building.

00:10:19.396 --> 00:10:20.698
He wasn't actually alive.

00:10:20.794 --> 00:10:22.254
Anyway, I'm going to move on.

00:10:22.292 --> 00:10:25.366
The footsteps lead to a dead end in her basement, then continue up the

00:10:25.388 --> 00:10:28.358
wall leading to where The Man Who Can’t Breathe stands upside down on the ceiling.

00:10:28.364 --> 00:10:30.642
He attempts to choke her and she screams.

00:10:30.706 --> 00:10:31.426
Guess she's afraid now.

00:10:31.458 --> 00:10:34.406
She's able to break away and run up the stairs to safety, but when she

00:10:34.428 --> 00:10:37.638
gets there, her sweater is torn, as if something had slashed through it.

00:10:37.724 --> 00:10:39.702
Like we've seen other entities do in the past.

00:10:39.756 --> 00:10:42.434
He's trying to scare her away, to prevent her from helping Quinn.

00:10:42.482 --> 00:10:44.982
The next day, he moves closer to taking Quinn's soul.

00:10:45.046 --> 00:10:48.266
During a video chat, her friend Maggie notices someone else in the room with

00:10:48.288 --> 00:10:49.990
her, but thinks that it's her brother, Alex.

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:53.146
Quinn eventually realizes that The Man Who Can’t Breathe is standing in her

00:10:53.168 --> 00:10:55.162
windowsill, staring intensely at her.

00:10:55.216 --> 00:10:58.798
He suddenly drops down under her bed, and when she goes to look, he instead

00:10:58.884 --> 00:11:01.310
grabs her from above and throws her out of the bed.

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:04.574
He calmly walks to the window and shuts out the light with the curtain, then

00:11:04.612 --> 00:11:07.230
closes the door, ensuring complete darkness in the room.

00:11:07.300 --> 00:11:10.334
He pins her down, but once again her dad comes to the rescue.

00:11:10.382 --> 00:11:13.486
And when he opened the door, light fills the room and

00:11:13.518 --> 00:11:14.638
The Man Who Can't Breathe disappears.

00:11:14.734 --> 00:11:18.274
However, this time he's able to take a piece of her soul with him, and this

00:11:18.312 --> 00:11:21.830
other half of her manifests in The Further as an incomplete version of her,

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:25.810
missing several key features like eyes, nose, mouth, hands and feet.

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:29.046
As the man takes more of her soul, the second Quinn would become more and

00:11:29.068 --> 00:11:29.766
more complete.

00:11:29.868 --> 00:11:33.802
I see this as a visual manifestation of her will to live. 

00:11:33.856 --> 00:11:37.226
As bad things continue to happen to her, such as losing her mom, failing to impress

00:11:37.248 --> 00:11:40.154
her dream school, and becoming physically disabled, she gets more and more

00:11:40.192 --> 00:11:43.286
depressed and gives more of her soul away to the Quinn in the darkness.

00:11:43.398 --> 00:11:46.782
At one point, she even tells her dad that she can no longer taste her food,

00:11:46.836 --> 00:11:50.010
which is an uncommon symptom of depression known as anhedonia.

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:53.038
She would meet the second Quinn shortly after. Wheezy comes down from the

00:11:53.044 --> 00:11:55.722
ceiling again and transports her to the abandoned fifth floor.

00:11:55.786 --> 00:11:59.074
It's never really spelled out for us if this happened while she was actually

00:11:59.112 --> 00:12:01.058
asleep, but I'm guessing that's the case.

00:12:01.144 --> 00:12:03.330
She comes to while she's alone for a moment.

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:06.338
We don't know why, but I can only imagine that he just wanted her to get her

00:12:06.344 --> 00:12:09.486
hopes up, that she might be able to escape, only to crush them by appearing

00:12:09.518 --> 00:12:12.806
behind her and wheeling her back into captivity, dumping her on the floor of

00:12:12.828 --> 00:12:15.458
apartment 514, and injuring her even further.

00:12:15.554 --> 00:12:19.394
She comes face to face with the alternate version of herself, and somehow

00:12:19.442 --> 00:12:22.726
Quinn's banging on the floor, gets the attention of her dad below, and he

00:12:22.748 --> 00:12:24.278
comes to the rescue with a flashlight.

00:12:24.374 --> 00:12:27.610
The Man Who Can’t Breathe creates an illusion that he was actually a crazy

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:30.762
man who jumped out the window, causing Sean to follow a new set of black

00:12:30.816 --> 00:12:33.594
footprints to the window and see what looks like a terminal patient

00:12:33.642 --> 00:12:34.922
splattered on the sidewalk.

00:12:34.986 --> 00:12:38.394
However, this is only a fake out, because when Quinn looks over, she sees

00:12:38.442 --> 00:12:39.920
something much different.

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:45.674
Her dad is able to pull her to safety and later tries to recruit Elise,

00:12:45.722 --> 00:12:49.410
which the demon is probably aware of, but Elise is unable to make it to him.

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:52.818
She's going through a depression arc of her own after losing her husband the

00:12:52.824 --> 00:12:56.050
year before and being attacked by a different entity while trying to contact

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:56.862
him in The Further.

00:12:56.926 --> 00:13:00.598
So instead, self proclaimed ghost hunters Specs and Tucker outfit Quinn with

00:13:00.604 --> 00:13:03.506
a night vision camera, and hours later, they observe The Man Who Can't Breathe

00:13:03.538 --> 00:13:06.770
most likely moving this camera and hiding it in the closet.

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:09.926
At this point, the evil entity seems to have enough of Quinn's soul to

00:13:09.948 --> 00:13:11.042
possess her temporarily.

00:13:11.106 --> 00:13:14.262
In Insidious 1, we saw The Red Face Demon essentially puppetting Dalton,

00:13:14.326 --> 00:13:16.650
but I don't think that's necessarily what's happening here.

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:19.786
Quinn appears behind them and manages to kick Tucker to the ground with her

00:13:19.808 --> 00:13:22.854
broken leg, beat down her dad with the pipe branch, and then knocks Specs

00:13:22.902 --> 00:13:24.150
down with a single swing.

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:26.174
Insidious 3 came out a couple years before

00:13:26.212 --> 00:13:29.226
We would see something similar in Cult of Chucky, where the voodoo possessed

00:13:29.258 --> 00:13:31.882
Nica is able to walk on two paraplegic legs.

00:13:31.946 --> 00:13:33.294
It's probably the same idea, though.

00:13:33.332 --> 00:13:36.622
The possession is literally just a means of taking a body and manipulating it.

00:13:36.686 --> 00:13:41.704
So it's pretty clear that it's the demon talking, not Quinn, when she says this

00:13:41.704 --> 00:13:43.890
-[Quinn/Demon] Very useless ******* father.

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:46.980
-[Quinn/Demon] Your wife had to die to get away from you.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:49.266
-[Quinn/Demon] Now I'd rather be dead too.

00:13:49.368 --> 00:13:52.610
It's quite possible that Sean is already lined up as the next target.

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:55.878
The Man Who Can’t Breathe will keep causing pain and continually turn the

00:13:55.884 --> 00:13:58.790
cycle of depression in order to collect more and more souls.

00:13:58.870 --> 00:14:02.698
With that, his use for Quinn in the world of the living was no more.

00:14:02.864 --> 00:14:03.580
-[Sean] No. Noooooooo!!! 

00:14:04.805 --> 00:14:07.898
(Impact)

00:14:09.607 --> 00:14:13.230
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:16.894
As the possessed, Quinn tried to delete her own file by bringing a box

00:14:16.932 --> 00:14:17.754
cutter to her neck.

00:14:17.802 --> 00:14:19.262
She was seized by Specs and Mr. Brenner.

00:14:19.316 --> 00:14:22.586
We see her try to run up the wall like what happened in Elise's basement,

00:14:22.618 --> 00:14:25.642
but they stop her and pin her down on the bed, where an eyeball

00:14:25.706 --> 00:14:28.478
travels up her throat and stares at them through her open mouth.

00:14:28.574 --> 00:14:32.066
The only logical interpretation that I have of this moment is that this is

00:14:32.088 --> 00:14:35.262
part of the process by which the second Quinn gains new features.

00:14:35.326 --> 00:14:38.382
This could also maybe explain the backwards face lady that we saw earlier.

00:14:38.446 --> 00:14:41.494
Maybe her soul was being reassembled in The Further and got put back

00:14:41.532 --> 00:14:42.630
together the wrong way.

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:45.766
They're able to restrain Quinn, which temporarily puts a hold on 

00:14:45.788 --> 00:14:48.070
The Man Who Can't Breathe being able to do anything in the real world.

00:14:48.140 --> 00:14:51.126
However, Elise shows up and explains that he's feeding on Quinn's life

00:14:51.148 --> 00:14:54.086
force to get stronger, and that with half of her soul already absorbed,

00:14:54.118 --> 00:14:56.410
they'll need to hurry to prevent him from taking all of it.

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:59.366
She goes into The Further and knows she's in the right place when she finds

00:14:59.398 --> 00:15:02.458
the doorknob covered in black tar, which seems to cover everything that the

00:15:02.464 --> 00:15:03.302
Demon touches.

00:15:03.366 --> 00:15:06.354
However, he is prepared with a plan for dealing with Elise.

00:15:06.422 --> 00:15:09.146
He presents in the form of her late husband, Jack.

00:15:09.258 --> 00:15:12.186
Not only is The Man Who Can’t Breathe knowledgeable enough to be familiar

00:15:12.218 --> 00:15:15.326
with the weaknesses of those who oppose him, but he also shows that he's a

00:15:15.348 --> 00:15:17.066
master of emotional manipulation.

00:15:17.178 --> 00:15:20.254
At the beginning, he knows that Quinn is desperate to talk to her mother,

00:15:20.302 --> 00:15:23.378
and uses that to his advantage to try to trick her into believing that the

00:15:23.384 --> 00:15:25.378
paranormal activity was coming from her.

00:15:25.464 --> 00:15:28.658
Now he's using the fact that he knows that Elise tried searching for Jack in

00:15:28.664 --> 00:15:31.874
The Further to convince her to take her own life using the shapeshifting form.

00:15:31.922 --> 00:15:35.234
However, he does leave a clue about his true identity.

00:15:35.362 --> 00:15:37.446
-[Jack/Demon] Stop breathing in it. Like I did.

00:15:37.548 --> 00:15:40.726
After she strikes him back with his own blade, he retreats into the dark and

00:15:40.748 --> 00:15:42.950
reemerges in his true cancerous form.

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:46.346
With a clap, he summons the copy of Quinn, who has now gained a nose, a

00:15:46.368 --> 00:15:47.270
mouth, and feet.

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:50.598
Elise pushes the Demon away to try to escape with Quinn's fragmented soul.

00:15:50.614 --> 00:15:53.926
But a powerful stomp tosses the whole room into disarray, and a dresser

00:15:53.958 --> 00:15:54.998
knocks them to the ground.

00:15:55.094 --> 00:15:58.014
Still, he gets chased to the elevator, but cannot get there in time to stop

00:15:58.052 --> 00:15:58.552
the two.

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:01.726
But this entity doesn't really need the elevator, thanks to his ability to

00:16:01.748 --> 00:16:03.722
travel through the vents and along walls.

00:16:03.786 --> 00:16:06.750
He cuts them off and throws Elise down the hall with a single hand.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:10.306
Before caressing Quinn, we can see how he's creating the false promise of

00:16:10.328 --> 00:16:13.074
nurturement for her, which is part of what she's been missing in her life

00:16:13.112 --> 00:16:14.494
ever since her mother's passing.

00:16:14.542 --> 00:16:18.674
He wants her to give up on life and come over to... the dark side.

00:16:18.792 --> 00:16:22.162
But as I mentioned, Elise had just been through her own state of depression,

00:16:22.226 --> 00:16:25.318
retiring from the paranormal business after being threatened by The Bride in Black.

00:16:25.324 --> 00:16:28.806
But she comes out of her shell when she sees Quinn, who has so much

00:16:28.828 --> 00:16:32.166
more life to live, falling into the same rut and nearly giving up her

00:16:32.188 --> 00:16:33.190
soul because of it.

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:35.958
Elise strikes back with a stomp of her own, sending The Man Who Can't Breathe

00:16:35.974 --> 00:16:37.302
crashing through the floor,

00:16:37.366 --> 00:16:39.306
but as always, he quickly gets back to them

00:16:39.328 --> 00:16:42.586
before Quinn has a chance to rejoin with her body and the other half of her soul.

00:16:42.608 --> 00:16:46.234
He takes hold of her and strokes her hair, all in a very motherly fashion.

00:16:46.282 --> 00:16:49.742
As he consumes more of her, The Further version of her gains hands

00:16:49.796 --> 00:16:50.474
and fingers.

00:16:50.522 --> 00:16:53.774
He's on the verge of taking her in full when another spirit shows up.

00:16:53.812 --> 00:16:56.638
It's Lily Brenner, only this time, it's really her.

00:16:56.724 --> 00:16:59.602
She whispers something to Quinn which seems to awaken her.

00:16:59.656 --> 00:17:03.122
Now, with fully formed eyes, she removes the oxygen mask from his face,

00:17:03.176 --> 00:17:06.194
causing some kind of liquid to gush through the gaping hole that is his mouth.

00:17:06.232 --> 00:17:09.794
To me, this symbolizes all of the life force that he had stolen from

00:17:09.832 --> 00:17:12.982
her and possibly all of the others that he had captured, spilling out,

00:17:13.036 --> 00:17:16.294
allowing her to be free of his grasp and return to her own world.

00:17:16.412 --> 00:17:19.766
There is a sense of finality to his encounter with Quinn, and if I had to

00:17:19.788 --> 00:17:22.242
guess, this is the death of The Man Who Can’t Breathe.

00:17:22.306 --> 00:17:25.626
However, I wouldn't be shocked to learn he survived and moved on to a new target.

00:17:25.648 --> 00:17:28.918
But at the end of the day, that's just my interpretation.

00:17:29.014 --> 00:17:32.218
The Man Who Can’t Breathe is a character we don't see much of even in the

00:17:32.224 --> 00:17:33.070
scenes he's in.

00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:36.154
Unlike the other antagonists in the series, his background is mostly unknown.

00:17:36.202 --> 00:17:40.026
I think the designer of his character's look put it perfectly.

00:17:40.467 --> 00:17:45.626
-[Justin] I think it's always better to have something for your imagination and hide

00:17:45.658 --> 00:17:48.674
-[Justin] it and not put something right in front of you, right in your face.

00:17:48.792 --> 00:17:52.226
-[Justin] I think the best horror movies are you keep it in the dark, you show a

00:17:52.248 --> 00:17:56.050
-[Justin] little bit and let the imagination of the audience go from there.

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:58.958
That's how the horror scenes are handled and that's how the lore surrounding

00:17:58.974 --> 00:18:01.666
him is handled, leaving The Man Who Can’t Breathe as one of the biggest

00:18:01.698 --> 00:18:04.018
mysteries from the career of Elise Rainier.

00:18:04.114 --> 00:18:07.046
But to fully appreciate the world of Insidious and The Further you need to

00:18:07.068 --> 00:18:08.930
understand the stories of its inhabitants.

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:10.742
So click on that playlist on the left.

00:18:10.796 --> 00:18:13.770
And if you love horror, remember to subscribe to CZsWorld

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:14.956
for new horrors every week.

00:18:14.956 --> 00:18:18.694
Ring the death bell for all notifications, and I will see you in the next one,

00:18:19.300 --> 00:18:22.133
assuming we both survive.

